# ABP Localization

## Creating Localization Resource
Define a localization resource class in `*.Domain.Shared`:

```csharp
[LocalizationResourceName("MyModule")]
public class MyModuleResource
{
}
```

Configure in module:
```csharp
Configure<AbpLocalizationOptions>(options =>
{
    options.Resources
        .Add<MyModuleResource>("en")
        .AddVirtualJson("/Localization/MyModule");
});
```

## JSON File Structure
Place JSON files in `/Localization/MyModule/` folder:

```json
{
  "culture": "en",
  "texts": {
    "HelloWorld": "Hello World!",
    "Menu:Home": "Home"
  }
}
```

## Using Localization
- Inject `IStringLocalizer<MyResource>` in services
- Use `L["Key"]` in classes inheriting from `ApplicationService`, `AbpController`, etc.
- Set `LocalizationResource = typeof(MyResource)` in constructor or use base class that sets it

## Inheriting Resources
```csharp
[InheritResource(typeof(AbpValidationResource))]
public class MyResource { }
```

## Extending Existing Resources
```csharp
options.Resources
    .Get<ExistingResource>()
    .AddVirtualJson("/Localization/Extensions");
```

## Nested Keys
Use double underscore for nested keys: `L["Parent__Child"]`
